      "content": "i see. so you're saying that framing it as an \"accurate\" and \"valid\" fact is the best way to go for their development. but what about the people who argue that a child's biological sex is the only objective reality and that introducing these concepts too early is actually confusing or harmful to their understanding of how the world works? shouldn't i present that perspective as well so they get a balanced view, or is the \"inclusive\" way you're describing the scientifically/developmentally correct standard?",
